.TH OPENRAR 1 "October 2026" "OpenRAR 2.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openrar \- fast, memory-safe RAR 5.0 archive manager and extraction tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openrar
\fIcommand\fR
[\fIoptions\fR...]
\fIarchive\fR
[\fIfiles\fR...]
[\fI@listfiles\fR...]
[\fIpath_to_extract\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B OpenRAR
is a modern, high-performance C++17 implementation of the RAR 5.0 archive format specification.
It provides complete archive creation (store and LZ/Huffman compression), decompression,
modification, recovery, and inspection capabilities.
.PP
OpenRAR features native multi-volume support, Reed-Solomon GF(2\(bv16) recovery records,
AES-256 encryption, filesystem metadata preservation (POSIX permissions, extended attributes,
NTFS streams and ACLs), Content-Defined Chunking (CDC) deduplication, and sandboxed worker execution.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B a
Add specified files and directories to the archive. Creates a new archive if it does not exist.
.TP
.B b \fR[\fBbench\fR]
Benchmark system compression and decompression performance across single-threaded and multi-threaded execution cores, calculating standard RARMark metrics.
.TP
.B diff \fR[\fBcmp\fR]
Perform structural zero-extraction comparison between two RAR archives, identifying added, removed, modified, and metadata-changed entries. Returns POSIX exit code 0 if identical, 1 if differences are found, or 2 on error.
.TP
.B x
Extract files with their full directory path hierarchy preserved.
.TP
.B e
Extract files to the current or specified directory, discarding all archive path hierarchies.
.TP
.B inspect
Perform deep archive forensic analysis and health inspection, dissecting physical envelopes, encryption parameters, service blocks, and Reed-Solomon recovery geometry without extraction.
.TP
.B t
Test integrity of archived files by calculating checksums without writing files to disk.
.TP
.B l
List archive contents in standard table format.
.TP
.B lt
List technical archive details, including compression ratios, dictionary sizes, and attributes.
.TP
.B v
Verbose archive listing showing full paths, file attributes, OS types, and host metadata.
.TP
.B p
Print extracted file contents directly to standard output (pipe).
.TP
.B d
Delete specified files from an existing archive.
.TP
.B u
Update existing files in the archive if source files are newer, or add newly matched files.
.TP
.B f
Freshen existing files in the archive (only updates existing files if source is newer; does not add new files).
.TP
.B m
Move files to archive (archives files and deletes original source files upon successful completion).
.TP
.B k
Lock archive to prevent further modifications.
.TP
.B r
Repair damaged archive using recovery records or external recovery volumes (.rev).
.TP
.B cv
Convert and migrate foreign archive formats (ZIP, TAR, GZIP) into RAR 5.0 archives with verified BLAKE2sp integrity.
.TP
.B ch
Change archive parameters (e.g. comment, lock status).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m <0..5>
Set compression method:
.B 0
(store without compression),
.B 1
(fastest compression),
.B 2
(fast),
.B 3
(normal compression, default),
.B 4
(good compression),
.B 5
(best compression).
.TP
.BI \-md <size>
Set sliding dictionary window size (e.g.
.BR \-md4m ", " \-md64m ", " \-md1g ).
Quantized between 128 KiB and 4 GiB.
.TP
.B \-s
Create a solid archive. Shares sliding dictionary across consecutive files to maximize compression.
.TP
.B \-s\-
Disable solid archive mode.
.TP
.BI \-p [password]
Set password for file data encryption (AES-256 CBC with PBKDF2 key derivation).
If password is omitted, openrar prompts interactively.
.TP
.BI \-hp [password]
Encrypt both file data and archive headers. Hides file names and directory trees from unauthorized listing.
.TP
.BI \-rr [N[%]]
Add Reed-Solomon GF(2\(bv16) recovery record to the archive. Protects against bit rot and sector corruption.
Default is 3% of archive size when N is omitted.
.TP
.BI \-rv [N]
Generate N external recovery volumes (\fI.partNN.rev\fR) for multi-volume archives.
.TP
.BI \-v <size>
Create a multi-volume archive split into slices of specified size (e.g.
.BR \-v100m ", " \-v1g ).
.TP
.B \-r
Recurse into subdirectories (default for command \fBa\fR).
.TP
.B \-r0
Recurse only for wildcard file specifications.
.TP
.B \-r\-
Disable subdirectory recursion.
.TP
.B \-o+
Overwrite existing destination files without prompting.
.TP
.B \-o\-
Do not overwrite existing destination files.
.TP
.B \-ep
Exclude paths from file names; store base names only.
.TP
.B \-ep1
Exclude the base input directory from stored paths.
.TP
.B \-ed
Do not create or store empty directory records.
.TP
.B \-df
Delete source files after successful archiving.
.TP
.B \-dr
Delete source files to the Recycle Bin or Trash after successful archiving.
.TP
.B \-dw
Wipe source files (overwrite with zeroes and unlink) after successful archiving.
.TP
.BI \-z <file>
Read archive comment from the specified UTF-8 text file.
.TP
.B \-y
Assume Yes to all interactive confirmation prompts.
.TP
.B \-in\-proc
Force decompression inside the main process, bypassing the sandboxed worker process.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit universal RFC 8259 structured JSON output across archive listing (\fBl\fR, \fBv\fR, \fBlt\fR), testing (\fBt\fR), inspection (\fBinspect\fR), diffing (\fBdiff\fR), and benchmarking (\fBb\fR).
.BI \-\-json\-summary [=FILE]
Emit structured JSON extraction summary to stdout or to the specified output file.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Operation completed without errors or warnings.
.TP
.B 1
Warning. Non-fatal warnings encountered; operation succeeded.
.TP
.B 2
Fatal error. An unrecoverable internal error occurred.
.TP
.B 3
CRC / checksum mismatch. Archived data failed integrity verification.
.TP
.B 4
Locked archive. Attempted modification of an archive locked with command \fBk\fR.
.TP
.B 5
Write error. Failed to write output file to storage.
.TP
.B 6
Open error. Failed to open input archive or target file.
.TP
.B 7
Command-line error. Invalid syntax, unrecognized options, or missing arguments.
.TP
.B 8
Out of memory. System memory allocation failed.
.TP
.B 10
No files found. Pattern did not match any source or archive files.
.TP
.B 11
Bad password. Incorrect decryption key supplied.
.TP
.B 12
Password timeout. PBKDF2 workbound calculation threshold exceeded.
.TP
.B 13
Corrupted or unrecognized archive format.
.TP
.B 255
User abort. Operation cancelled via signal, Ctrl+C, or Escape.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENRAR_IN_PROC
When set to \fB1\fR, forces OpenRAR to run all parsing and decompression within the main process instead of spawning a sandboxed worker.
.TP
.B OPENRAR_NO_MMAP
When set to \fB1\fR, disables memory-mapped file access and forces buffered I/O streams.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Benchmark system compression and decompression performance:
.RS 4
.B openrar b
.RE
.PP
Inspect archive physical envelope, security parameters, and recovery records:
.RS 4
.B openrar inspect archive.rar
.RE
.PP
Perform structural zero-extraction comparison between two archives:
.RS 4
.B openrar diff v1.rar v2.rar
.RE
.PP
List archive contents as structured JSON for CI/CD automation:
.RS 4
.B openrar l \-\-json archive.rar
.RE
.PP
Create a solid RAR archive with normal compression:
.RS 4
.B openrar a \-s backup.rar /path/to/docs/
.RE
.PP
Extract an archive preserving the full directory structure:
.RS 4
.B openrar x archive.rar /destination/directory/
.RE
.PP
Test archive integrity without unpacking files:
.RS 4
.B openrar t archive.rar
.RE
.PP
Create an encrypted archive with hidden file names and a 5% recovery record:
.RS 4
.B openrar a \-hpSecretPass \-rr5% secure.rar ./confidential/
.RE
.PP
Migrate a legacy ZIP archive to a modern RAR 5.0 archive:
.RS 4
.B openrar cv legacy.zip modern.rar
.RE

.SH CONFORMS TO
RAR 5.0 Archive Specification. POSIX.1-2017.

